BA_ "Description" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_TempVal "This is actual battery electrolyte temperature value by battery sensor.
The value is calculated by a Battery Temperature Model, depending on measured temperature of the battery pole.
The resolution is 0.5¡É.";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_TempVal 511;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_TempVal 7;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_TempVal 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_TempVal 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_TempVal "20.03.05";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SohVal "[For 12V Lithium Battery vehicle model]
This signal is battery State of Health(SOH) as calculated by battery sensor.
This value shows reduction rate of nominal capacity.
This value can be used for diagnosis information of application system.";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SohVal 127;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SohVal 7;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SohVal 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SohVal 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SohVal "17.11.00";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SnsrInvldSta "[For 12V Lithium Battery vehicle model]
This bit is Battery Sensor Invalid flag and setting condition is depending on Battery Sensor self diagnosis information.
 BS Invalid = 0 : BS is Valid Condition
 BS Invalid = 1 : BS is Invalid Condition";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SnsrInvldSta 1;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SnsrInvldSta 7;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SnsrInvldSta 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SnsrInvldSta 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SnsrInvldSta "17.11.00";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SofVal "[For 12V Lithium Battery vehicle model]
This signal is battery State of Function(SOF) as calculated by battery sensor.
This value shows information about the battery ability to crank the engine (both of warm & cold cranking).
This value is prediction value of the minimum voltage for the next cranking.";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SofVal 127;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SofVal 7;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SofVal 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SofVal 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SofVal "17.11.00";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_RspErrSta "[For 12V Lithium Battery vehicle model]
Battery Sensor shall send one status bit signal, Response_Error. Response_Error shall be set whenever a frame received by the node or a frame transmitted by the node contains an error in the response field.
Response_Error shall be cleared after transmission.
Based on this single bit the master node can conclude the following:
 -Response_Error = 0 : the node is operating correctly
 -Response_Error = 1 : the node has intermittent problems
 -The node did not answer : the node (or bus or master) has serious problems.";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_RspErrSta 1;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_RspErrSta 7;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_RspErrSta 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_RspErrSta 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_RspErrSta "17.11.00";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_CapacityVal "12V Battery Capacity Value";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_CapacityVal 0;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_CapacityVal 7;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_CapacityVal 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_CapacityVal 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_CapacityVal "21.07.06";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SocErrSta "[For 12V Lithium Battery vehicle model]
This bit is flags for indication whether battery SOC detection value is plausible or not by battery sensor.
If it is set to value 0, then it means battery SOC is normal state.
If it is set to value 1, then it means battery SOC is implausible state.
 * Conditions to set value = 1
  1) There has no chance to recalibrate SOC after power on reset
  2) There has no SOC recalibration after last recalibration
  3) There has no chance to get a plausible CNOM value";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2227254530 BAT_SocErrSta 1;
