BA_ "Description" SG_ 2172674051 ESC_LongAccelOffstCalibPrmtr "This signal indicates information regarding the calibration parameter for longitudinal acceleration value.
This signal doesn't guarantee the actual offset value.
But this signal is the result of the measuring process about the offset which is the longitudinal acceleration value when the vehicle is on the flat ground.
(ÀÌ ½ÅÈ£´Â Â÷·®ÀÌ ÆòÆòÇÑ Áö¸é¿¡ ÀÖÀ» ¶§ Á¾¹æÇâ °¡¼Óµµ °ªÀÎ ¿É¼Â¿¡ ´ëÇÑ ÃøÁ¤ ÇÁ·Î¼¼½ºÀÇ °á°úÀÓ.)
Hence, the ECUs which receive this signal have to use this signal as substract from the longitudinal acceleration value from the sensor.
