BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_Crc4Val "The data area for CRC calculation is based on the data length (DLC) of the message DB.
The CRC shall be calculated over the entire data block (excluding the CRC bytes) including the user data, alive counter and Data ID
 
- CRC Polynomial (0x1021) , Initial Value : 0xFFFF, XOR value : 0x0000, Data ID : Message ID + 0xF800 
- The initial value is for CRC calculation and the message should be sent with the calculated result value. 
- The mathematical expression to 16 bit CRC polynomial is given here. G(x) = x16 + x12 + x5 + 1";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_Crc4Val 65535;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_Crc4Val 3;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_Crc4Val 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_Crc4Val 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_Crc4Val "18.11.08";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_AlvCnt4Val "For the first transmission request for a data element the counter shall be initialized with 0 and shall be incremented by 1 for every subsequent send request. 
When the counter reaches the maximum value(0xFF), then it shall restart with 0 for the next send request";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_AlvCnt4Val 0;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_AlvCnt4Val 3;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_AlvCnt4Val 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_AlvCnt4Val 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_AlvCnt4Val "18.11.08";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_TrgtGearSta "HTCU_TrgtGearSta informs about the speed, which is currently engaged in the gearbox, or, in case of a gear change (HTCU_GearChgSta), which speed is reached.
Note: Gear changes covering more than one speed are also possible.
In the P and N positions, the frictional connection is interrupted hydraulically.
Depending on the type of error, the 3rd or 4th (forward) speed, and the R (reverse) speed are engaged in the limp home program.";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_TrgtGearSta 0;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_TrgtGearSta 3;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_TrgtGearSta 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_TrgtGearSta 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_TrgtGearSta "18.12.07";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_RdySta "Flag that the HTCU is ready to work. (In fact, this flag is true from the moment that CAN is working. So, normally no ¡°false¡± will be sent on CAN.) This flag does not show that everything is alright in the HTCU. This information is given in the warning and fault flags.";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_RdySta 0;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_RdySta 3;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_RdySta 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_RdySta 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_RdySta "18.08.02";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_GearChgSta "HTCU_GearChgSta indicates whether a gear change is being executed in the gearbox.
Note : Gear change means a gear shift at D-range and Garage shift(PRND).";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_GearChgSta 0;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_GearChgSta 3;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_GearChgSta 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_GearChgSta 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_GearChgSta "18.08.02";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_TqRdctnPcVal "The HTCU requests a torque reduction via the signal CR_Tcu_TqInt_Pc to the ECU and MCU.
The requested torque HTCU_TqRdctnPcVal refers to a maximum torque CR_Ems_TqStd_Nm. This conversion into a physical quantity provides a range of CR_Ems_TqStd_Nm of 0 ..199.61%.
There is no specific phase relationship between the output and any other signal.
Conversion : (PH) = 0.390625 * (HEX) [%]";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_TqRdctnPcVal 511;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_TqRdctnPcVal 3;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_TqRdctnPcVal 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_TqRdctnPcVal 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_TqRdctnPcVal "18.08.02";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_FltSta "HTCU_FltSta informs about status of transmission control.

<Value Description>
Bit 0: HTCU Diagnostic failure
Bit 1: HTCU Diagnostic failure ? Limphome activated
Bit 2: OPU/EOP Diagnostic failure";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164278529 HTCU_FltSta 0;
