BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_Crc1Val "The data area for CRC calculation is based on the data length (DLC) of the message DB.
The CRC shall be calculated over the entire data block (excluding the CRC bytes) including the user data, alive counter and Data ID
 
- CRC Polynomial (0x1021) , Initial Value : 0xFFFF, XOR value : 0x0000, Data ID : Message ID + 0xF800 
- The initial value is for CRC calculation and the message should be sent with the calculated result value. 
- The mathematical expression to 16 bit CRC polynomial is given here. G(x) = x16 + x12 + x5 + 1";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_Crc1Val 65535;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_Crc1Val 3;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_Crc1Val 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_Crc1Val 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_Crc1Val "20.06.01";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_AlvCnt1Val "For the first transmission request for a data element the counter shall be initialized with 0 and shall be incremented by 1 for every subsequent send request. 
When the counter reaches the maximum value(0xFF), then it shall restart with 0 for the next send request";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_AlvCnt1Val 0;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_AlvCnt1Val 3;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_AlvCnt1Val 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_AlvCnt1Val 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_AlvCnt1Val "20.06.01";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_YawSigSta "This signal indicates failure status of yaw rate signal and yaw rate sensing element.

0000B : No failure 

xxx1B : IMU_Yawrate_failure

xx1xB : Initialization is running

x1xxB : Reserved

1xxxB : Reserved

This signal represents the physical error in MEMs sensor or microprocessor error in air bag control unit, but it does not contain the signal plausibility error check result. Signal plausibility error check has to be accomplished to each control unit using the own plausibility error check criterion.

The initialization time is the time that takes for the sensor to operate normally after power on. The maximum initialization time does not exceed the ACU CAN valid message transmission time. In the initial startup condition, the time does not exceed 1500ms and In case of ACU Only Reset, it does not 600ms.

The sensor status information is selected from one among 0000B, xxx1B, and xx1xB.";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_YawSigSta 2;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_YawSigSta 3;
BA_REL_ "GenSigTimeoutTime" BU_SG_REL_ PSB SG_ 2164279809 IMU_YawSigSta 500;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_YawSigSta 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_YawSigSta 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_YawSigSta "20.03.05";
