BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_McuVoltSta "This signal indicates the failure status of MCU.

0000B : No failure

xxx1B : MCU failure

xx1xB : Under voltage detected

x1xxB : Over voltage detected

1xxxB : Bus off failure

The status information(xxx1B) occurs when MCU error is detected or qualified. Low-voltage detected bit(xx1xB) and high-voltage detected bit(x1xxB) mean the vehicle ignition voltage status diagnosed by ACU, which do not indicate the MCU failure status.";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_McuVoltSta 0;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_McuVoltSta 3;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_McuVoltSta 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_McuVoltSta 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_McuVoltSta "20.03.05";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_AcuRstSta "This signal indicates the status of IMU.

0000B : Normal mode 

xxx1B : IMU Reset mode

xx1xB : Reserved

x1xxB : Reserved

1xxxB : Reserved

If ACU reset is required, ACU will send IMU RESET bit(XXX1B) up to 30 times and perform a reset. If RESET acknowledge signal is received from the ESC, the ACU interrupts the reset signal transmission and performs a reset immediately. Detailed logic follows ES95920-75.";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_AcuRstSta 0;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_AcuRstSta 3;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_AcuRstSta 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_AcuRstSta 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_AcuRstSta "20.03.05";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_SnsrTyp "This signal indicates supported signals that are correspond to sensor type.
0001B = IMU (yaw rate and lateral acceleration)
0010B = IMU (yaw rate, lateral and longitudinal acceleration)
0100B = IMU (yaw / roll rate, lateral and longitudinal acceleration)
1000B = IMU (yaw / roll rate, lateral, longitudinal and vertical acceleration)
All other values are reserved
¡Ø Initial value shall be actual value.
This signal indicates all sensor types available for the corresponding vehicle. whether to provide actual sensor information for each vehicle is determined according to a PEL (Product equipment list) component.";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164279809 IMU_SnsrTyp 2;
