BA_ "Description" SG_ 2164277251 TCU_ObdSta "The signal TCU_OBD is used to inform the OBD master (EMS-ECU) in case a OBD relevant fault is detected. According to the OBD regulations the TCU could request MIL on. If a freeze frame request by the TCU has not been acknowledged (OBD_FRF_ACK) within 2 seconds, this request has to be canceled.
-> Related signal : See ¡°EngFrzFrm¡± message
Bit0 : Reserved
Bit1 : Failure information of TCU
Bit2 : MIL on request

The exact meaning of this signals and under which conditions they are used has to be defined by the TCU supplier (in accordance with the OBD II regulations).";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2164277251 TCU_ObdSta 0;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2164277251 TCU_ObdSta 3;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2164277251 TCU_ObdSta 0;
